\par\par \uc2 REVIEW & OUTLOOK (Editorial)\par \b \uc2 The Real Green Energy Transition\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A16\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is showing what the real green-energy transition looks like: On Friday the auto maker announced plans to lay off 2,450 workers in Michigan as it ramps up electric-vehicle production. As consolation, the laid-off workers will receive a generous parting gift.\par \par \uc2 Car makers are struggling to sell higher-priced cars as consumers pull back after three years of inflation. At the same time, the rich labor agreement that \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , Ford and GM struck last autumn with the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  is raising costs. The companies need healthy profits from gas-powered trucks to subsidize their money-losing EV production.\par \par \uc2 Hence \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 's scramble to slash costs. The company last month announced buyouts for salaried workers in the U.S. On Friday it said it will lay off as many as 2,450 production workers in Warren, Mich., where it produces its classic Ram 1500 pickup, as it rolls out a new electric model. Workers can send a thank you card to \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain.\par \par \uc2 Car companies scrap old models all the time as they come out with new ones. But making EVs requires fewer workers than gas-powered cars, and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is seeking to take advantage of those manufacturing efficiencies. The problem, and the tragedy for the workers, is that such decisions are being driven by government mandates rather than market choices.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 's new emissions rules will effectively require companies to produce one to two electric trucks for every gas-powered truck as soon as 2027 and nearly four to one by 2032. California's mandates are even more aggressive and will ban the sale of new gas-powered cars by 2035.\par \par \uc2 Some 15 states have adopted California's EV quotas, including Minnesota, where Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  imposed them over strong opposition from his state's auto dealers. Kamala Harris also supported banning new gas-powered cars nationwide by 2035 when she ran for President in 2019. Does she still? Will anyone ask?\par \par \uc2 Democrats claim their green-energy transition will create millions of jobs, but the evidence so far suggests otherwise. The reality is that government will end up supporting workers who lose their jobs and can't find other work, which is why Democrats are pushing to expand the welfare state.\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is offering laid-off workers 52 weeks of unemployment assistance and 52 weeks of "transition assistance" plus two years of health coverage, on top of state unemployment benefits. That's generous, but many employers won't be able to afford such charity.\par \par \uc2 As government destroys more jobs, taxpayers will inevitably be asked to compensate for the damage.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240812ek8c0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
