\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  to Lay Off 2,450 Workers --- Plant in Michigan to end production of a Ram truck model and reduce shifts\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ben Glickman \par \uc2 471 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jeep\uc2 -maker \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  is laying off 2,450 factory workers in Michigan, after deciding to end production of a Ram truck model at a factory that has been making pickups for decades.\par \par \uc2 The move comes as the parent company's U.S. market share shrinks, dealers complain about an inventory buildup on their lots and the automaker prepares to roll out battery-powered models to match rivals.\par \par \uc2 The job cuts also follow a new labor deal reached last year by \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  that gave workers higher pay and better benefits, but also drove up labor costs for the European car company.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs could begin as early as Oct. 8 and the actual number could be lower if some workers transfer to other facilities, the company said.\par \par \uc2 The affected plant in Warren, Mich., which now has roughly 3,700 \uc2 UAW\uc2 -represented workers, will move from a two-shift to a one-shift operating pattern in general assembly, while other operations will remain on two shifts to support Jeep Wagoneer production.\par \par \uc2 In November of last year, the company introduced its new 2025 Ram 1500, a platform offering new options, including engine choice and electrification. With this new truck, it is killing off an older version of the Ram 1500, known as the Classic. \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  currently also makes Ram 1500 trucks at a facility in Sterling Heights, Mich., which is also near Detroit. Heavy-duty Ram trucks are built at an assembly plant in Saltillo, Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Carlos Tavares\uc2 , who has led \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  since it was formed in 2021 through the merger of France's \uc2 PSA Group\uc2  and \uc2 Fiat Chrysler Automobiles\uc2 , has sought to make the carmaker's operations more efficient to preserve profits.\par \par \uc2 The company has slimmed down its U.S. workforce multiple times in the past year, including cuts to its software and engineering divisions in March and a reduced shift at the company's Warren plant last month.\par \par \uc2 High sticker prices and aggressive production targets have led to an inventory buildup that is increasing the need for profit-damaging discounts. Some dealers have expressed frustration with the company's handling of the extra supply, arguing \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  hasn't done enough to make vehicles more affordable for consumers.\par \par \uc2 The company said with its first-half results that it would likely slash starting prices for its cars and trucks to clear out stock.\par \par \uc2 Surging car prices in the last several years led \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  to a boom in profit, allowing the company to pour billions in investment into new battery-powered offerings. Many of those new models are set to roll out to customers later this year.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Stephen Nakrosis contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240810ek8a0004m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
