\par\par \b \uc2 Paramount Writes Down Cable TV Unit, Cuts U.S. Workforce by 15%\b0\par\par\uc2 By Isabella Simonetti \par \uc2 571 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The slow-motion collapse of the cable-television business is coming into clearer focus.\par \par \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2 , home of channels including \uc2 Comedy Central\uc2 , \uc2 MTV\uc2  and Nickelodeon, on Thursday wrote down the value of its cable-TV networks by $6 billion, a day after rival \uc2 Warner Bros. Discovery\uc2  revised the worth of its own cable business lower by $9.1 billion.\par \par \uc2 Paramount is also cutting about 2,000 jobs, or 15% of its U.S. workforce, as part of an effort to realize $500 million in cost savings.\par \par \uc2 The reassessments by two of the country's largest TV conglomerates come as cable-TV networks are suffering from the acceleration of cord-cutting, declining ratings and a weak advertising market. Streaming platforms are taking audiences and subscribers away from what was once the engine powering the media industry.\par \par \uc2 "The challenges of the linear ecosystem are becoming even more apparent especially given the pressure on linear advertising and the competition for ad budgets with connected TV and streaming players and the increasing pressure with cord-cutting," said \uc2 Robert Fishman\uc2 , an analyst with MoffettNathanson.\par \par \uc2 During a call with investors to discuss the company's results, Chief Financial Officer \uc2 Naveen Chopra\uc2  said the write-down of the cable-TV business was triggered by the decline of the traditional TV business, as well as Paramount's recently announced deal to merge with \uc2 Skydance Media\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We need to reconcile the value of our individual reporting unit with the enterprise value for the entire company that's implied by the [Skydance] transaction," Chopra said.\par \par \uc2 Programmers are also facing pressure from distributors increasingly willing to play hardball when the time comes to renew carriage agreements. Earlier this year, customers of \uc2 Charter Communications\uc2 ' Spectrum TV service got free access to Paramount's ad-supported streaming services with their cable packages under a new distribution deal between the two companies. That agreement followed a similar model adopted after a high-profile feud between Charter and \uc2 Disney\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 Shares of Paramount were up 4.4% in after-hours trading.\par \par \uc2 Paramount, which also owns the namesake movie studio and the streaming services including Paramount+, said it lost $5.41 billion in the second quarter, largely due to the goodwill impairment charge it booked for its cable-networks unit. Revenue fell 11% to $6.81 billion.\par \par \uc2 The company said its streaming business -- which beyond Paramount+ also includes Pluto TV -- reported its first-ever quarterly profit. But Paramount+ lost 2.8 million subscribers in the quarter, which the company attributed to the exit from a hard bundle agreement in South Korea. The company reiterated its forecast that Paramount+ would be profitable domestically in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2 , one of Paramount's rivals, also reported streaming profitability for the first time earlier this week, one quarter ahead of schedule.\par \par \uc2 Revenue in Paramount's filmed entertainment business fell by 18%, the company said. Theatrical revenues suffered from the comparison with the year-earlier quarter, when "Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" was released.\par \par \uc2 Paramount is currently being run by "the office of the CEO" made up of its three divisional heads -- \uc2 Chris McCarthy\uc2 , \uc2 George Cheeks\uc2  and \uc2 Brian Robbins\uc2 . The CEOs earlier this year said the company's goal was to reach $500 million in annual cost savings.\par \par \uc2 To realize these savings, Paramount is reducing its U.S.-based workforce by approximately 15%.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich309\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal4635
