\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Spirit Furloughs Hundreds of Pilots --- Airline reports a wider loss for its second quarter, as it moves to cut costs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dean Seal and Victor Stefanescu \par \uc2 488 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Spirit Airlines\uc2  is furloughing hundreds of pilots as the airline industry's fight for passengers weighs on its bottom line.\par \par \uc2 The budget airline said Thursday that it was furloughing about 240 pilots and downgrading about 100 captains to cut costs. \uc2 Spirit\uc2  is also suspending the recruitment of pilots and flight attendants to reduce training expenses. Some flight attendants are being offered voluntary unpaid leaves of absence.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Ted Christie\uc2  said competition among airlines has hit a fever pitch after they increased capacity to meet higher demand. But those efforts outstripped demand and it resulted in a glut of empty airline seats, and carriers ramped up discounts to fill them. Despite the busy summer-travel season, a number of airlines, including \uc2 Delta Air Lines\uc2  and \uc2 American Airlines\uc2 , have posted weaker profits.\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 Spirit\uc2 , its losses ballooned in the second quarter and were larger than analysts had expected. It recorded a loss of $192.9 million in the three months ended June 30, compared with a loss of $2.3 million in the same quarter a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Revenue fell 11% to $1.28 billion, missing analysts' projections for $1.33 billion, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fred Cromer, the airline's new chief financial officer, said revenue projections for the third quarter don't offer the airline any relief.\par \par \uc2 "It's going to get worse before it gets better," Cromer said.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Spirit fell more than 8% in Thursday trading. In the past year, they have plummeted nearly 85%.\par \par \uc2 Spirit\uc2 's nonticket revenue has come under pressure since the ultralow-cost carrier cut certain prices and stopped charging for change and cancellation fees.\par \par \uc2 Large airlines have also introduced lower-cost services that compete with the airline's options, Christie said, adding that low-fare travel isn't broken.\par \par \uc2 The airline is adding travel options with perks such as included snacks, alcohol, internet connection and blocked middle seats. The options will go on sale on Aug. 16, Christie said, but he anticipates that it will take passengers time to adopt the changes. \uc2 Spirit\uc2  has also spent the past year overhauling its network in a bid to better match seasonal and daily demand.\par \par \uc2 "That means we need patience from our constituents and adequate liquidity to navigate" the environment," he said.\par \par \uc2 For the current quarter, \uc2 Spirit\uc2  expects to generate $1.16 billion to $1.18 billion in revenue, down from $1.43 billion in the year prior. Analysts polled by \uc2 FactSet\uc2  had been expecting a smaller drop to $1.33 billion.\par \par \uc2 Spirit\uc2 's disappointing results come in the same week that \uc2 JetBlue Airways\uc2  reported a surprise adjusted profit for the second quarter as it cut unprofitable flights from its network and leaned into pockets of heavy demand, such as leisure travel in New England.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240802ek820001i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
