\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Contractor Sued Over Migrant Children Abuse\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michelle Hackman \par \uc2 429 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- Unaccompanied migrant children in the government's custody have been repeatedly sexually abused over the last decade by employees of the contractor providing them shelter care, according to a lawsuit filed by the Justice Department.\par \par \uc2 The suit alleges that Austin, Texas-based Southwest Key Programs, a nonprofit shelter operator that runs the largest number of migrant child shelters across the country, is responsible for years of "severe, pervasive" sexual abuse and harassment of children as young as 5 years old. The Justice Department's action comes after the government tried to punish the operator for individual cases.\par \par \uc2 "In some cases, Southwest Key employees threatened children to maintain their silence," the Justice Department wrote in its suit filed Wednesday night. "In harassing these children, these Southwest Key employees exploited the children's vulnerabilities, language barriers, and distance from family and loved ones."\par \par \uc2 The operator's spokeswoman, Anais Biera Miracle, said: "Southwest Key Programs' primary focus is the safety, health, and well-being of each one of the children and youth we care for."\par \par \uc2 "We continue to review the complaint, and it does not present the accurate picture of the care and commitment our employees provide to the youth and children," she said.\par \par \uc2 Employees allegedly raped children, solicited sex acts and pushed children to take nude photos in documented cases spanning from 2015 through 2023, the suit says.\par \par \uc2 In one instance in 2022, a youth-care worker in El Paso, Texas, repeatedly entered the bedrooms of children as young as 5 years old in the middle of the night and touched their "private area," and threatened to kill the children's families if they disclosed the abuse to anyone else, the suit says.\par \par \uc2 In another, in 2019, a supervisor at a shelter in Channelview, Texas, repeatedly raped a teenage girl and demanded she take videos touching herself, the suit says She reported the abuse only when the employee went on an international vacation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  is responsible for housing unaccompanied children -- predominantly from Guatemala, El Salvador, Honduras or Mexico -- while they wait to be placed with adult guardians more permanently in the U.S. Rather than run its own shelters, the government contracts with private shelter providers, and Southwest Key houses a large proportion of migrant children in the government's care at any given time.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department says Southwest Key has violated the Fair Housing Act, a 1960s-era civil-rights law, by failing to provide children a safe living environment.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240719ek7j0001k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
