\par\par \b \uc2 Dockworkers, Ports in a Standoff as Strike Threats Grow\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Berger \par \uc2 606 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 July 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The U.S. is facing potential disruptions at major seaports for the second time in as many years.\par \par \uc2 Harold Daggett, the head of the union that represents dockworkers at East Coast and Gulf Coast ports, is warning that time is running out to secure a new longshore labor deal before the current multiyear contract expires Sept. 30. and that a strike "is becoming more likely."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Longshoremen's Association\uc2 , which represents about 45,000 workers at ports from Maine to Texas, abruptly withdrew from the talks in June just as they were set to begin, citing a dispute over the use of automation. No new negotiations have been set.\par \par \uc2 Shipping industry executives, who have grown used to Daggett's bellicose rhetoric, until recently believed the strike warnings he started making last year were a negotiating tactic.\par \par \uc2 But some executives are beginning to speak of how long a strike could last rather than if it will happen.\par \par \uc2 An October walkout would hit some of the country's biggest ports, including New York and New Jersey, Virginia and Savannah, Ga., at the busiest time of year for shipping, when retailers are bringing in holiday-season goods. It would also provide a political headache for President Biden five weeks ahead of the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Biden administration officials last summer helped broker a deal in stalled longshore labor talks on the West Coast that had dragged on for more than a year and that were marked by dockworker disruptions in California and Washington state.\par \par \uc2 The ILA warned July 12 that it didn't want anyone, including Biden administration officials, "to interfere in our negotiations."\par \par \uc2 To get a deal, the union and shipping executives still have to resolve several issues specific to local ports. They also remain far apart on a coastwide increase in wages.\par \par \uc2 People familiar with the talks say Daggett is pushing for a much higher pay increase than the 32% raise over six years secured by West Coast dockworkers.\par \par \uc2 Ocean carriers made billions of dollars in profits during the Covid pandemic when shipping rates soared. "You made millions and billions of dollars in the last five, six years off the sweat of our backs," Daggett said at an ILA convention last summer. "Don't come back and say we can't afford that kind of raise."\par \par \uc2 The ILA walked away from the scheduled start of negotiations in June, saying it had discovered that a container-handling terminal at Alabama's Port of Mobile was using automated equipment to process trucks.\par \par \uc2 Mobile is an unlikely flashpoint for a dispute that now threatens to imperil trade at ports from Maine to Texas. Measured by the number of boxes it moves per year, the port ranks outside the top 10 ports on the East Coast and Gulf Coast.\par \par \uc2 Daggett fiercely opposes automation at ports. But people familiar with the labor talks say the truck-processing technology has been in operation at Mobile since 2008 and that the ILA hadn't previously pointed to it as a problem.\par \par \uc2 ILA spokesman James McNamara said on Wednesday that use of the technology for more than 15 years "doesn't make it right if it violated the master contract." McNamara said the union believes the same technology is being used at other ports in violation of the contract.\par \par \uc2 The ILA says it won't resume talks until the issue at Mobile and other ports is resolved. Daggett has also said he won't extend the current labor agreement when it expires this fall and that dockworkers won't work without a contract.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240718ek7i0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
