\par\par \b \uc2 Musk Scores Win Over Ex-Employees Of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  in Severance-Pay Lawsuit\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alyssa Lukpat \par \uc2 431 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 July 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A federal judge dismissed a lawsuit against \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and his social-media company that claimed thousands of laid-off \uc2 Twitter\uc2  employees weren't paid at least $500 million in severance.\par \par \uc2 The judge in California's northern district said this week that the lawsuit by two ex-employees of \uc2 Twitter\uc2  incorrectly claimed the company's severance plan was governed by a federal law dictating minimum payment thresholds.\par \par \uc2 Judge Trina Thompson said the former employees would have three weeks to refile their claims, potentially giving them another opportunity to sue Musk and the company, now known as X.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is one of several related to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  layoffs and severance payments after Musk bought the company in 2022 for $44 billion. \uc2 Twitter\uc2 's former chief executive, \uc2 Parag Agrawal\uc2 , and three other top executives sued the company this year, saying Musk owed them $128 million in severance. Musk, who has been accused of not paying bills he owes to landlords, vendors and others, has denied wrongdoing, saying he fired the executives for cause.\par \par \uc2 Musk cut many \uc2 Twitter\uc2  employees after buying the company. He said in April 2023 that the company had about 1,500 employees, down from around 8,000. Musk renamed the company and upended norms in the organization.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire, who also is CEO of electric-vehicle maker \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and rocket company \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , is currently the world's richest person, with a net worth valued at about $274 billion, according to \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 's billionaires index.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, which was dismissed on Tuesday, was filed in July 2023 by former employee Courtney McMillian, \uc2 Twitter\uc2 's former head of people experience. Ronald Cooper, a workplace operations, facilities and people manager, joined the lawsuit several months later. The two were seeking class-action status.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for McMillian and Cooper said, "We are disappointed in the ruling and considering our options for moving forward."\par \par \uc2 The company and lawyers for X and Musk didn't immediately return requests for comment Thursday.\par \par \uc2 McMillian and Cooper said in their lawsuit that they were offered only a month of severance pay when they were entitled to more under the company's severance plan. They said the company's failure to make further payments violated the Employee Retirement Income Security Act, a federal law that outlines severance plan guidelines.\par \par \uc2 X said the severance plan wasn't governed by that law and it had no continuing administrative program for the payments as required under Erisa.\par \par \uc2 Judge Thompson agreed with the social-media company and dismissed the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240712ek7c0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
