\par\par \uc2 REVIEW & OUTLOOK (Editorial)\par \b \uc2 A Union Strikes Against -- the Union\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 One of our favorite cartoons has a boss saying to a worker in front of his desk something like, "I'm going to stick it to the man." To which the worker replies, "But you are the man."\par \par \uc2 We thought of that cartoon Friday when we heard about the latest \uc2 National Education Association\uc2  strike -- no, not against some poor public school district. We mean the strike this week by NEA employees against their own union.\par \par \uc2 America's largest labor union has a problem with its proletariat. Union staff walked out of the NEA's annual national meeting on Friday at Philadelphia's convention center. The National Education Association Staff Organization (Neaso) -- a union within the union, which represents employees against the bosses -- has filed unfair labor-practice complaints with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The staff union says the parent union wrongly halted overtime pay for holidays. It also accuses their bosses of contracting out $50 million of work without adequately informing members. Et tu, comrade?\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 National Education Association\uc2  has threatened to host its convention virtually to avoid a physical picket line. For a union to trick its members into crossing a picket line is reprehensible," said Neaso president Robin McLean. "It also confirms what we have been saying: NEA has abandoned its union values with its actions at the bargaining table."\par \par \uc2 Where's the Biden \uc2 NLRB\uc2  when you need it? For that matter, why aren't Bernie Sanders and President Biden at the picket line?\par \par \uc2 The convention was supposed to be a pep rally for Mr. Biden, who was scheduled to address the delegates Sunday to remind teachers of all the money he has bestowed on them. But scenes of picketing teachers and a partly empty convention hall wouldn't be a good look for an already beleaguered campaign. The President canceled Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 The NEA, with some three million members, is a political power that like many unions is straying these days into other left-wing causes. The current NEA convention is thick with anti-Israel protesters. Progressive members are pushing the union to call for a cease-fire in Gaza, and they planned to harangue Mr. Biden to withhold aid to Israel.\par \par \uc2 It's certainly amusing to see the well-paid bosses at the NEA called out by the rank-and-file for collective-bargaining abuses. NEA president \uc2 Becky Pringle\uc2 's pay last year was $495,787, according to Americans for Fair Treatment. Upstanding teachers may learn something about their bosses' priorities from the labor standoff. Too bad they don't strike against the NEA's immoral defense of failing public schools.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240706ek760001y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
